(7301313, 1137926, 19959, '<td valign="top">I agree with the comment.. This was the worst day for sun-set.. I have a far better shot from later in the week but was outside of the challenge window ...</td>', 'I agree with the comment.. This was the worst day for sun-set.. I have a far better shot from later in the week but was outside of the challenge window ...', '2015-01-12 07:27:38.000000', NULL, 0),
(7304624, 1138267, 49018, '<td valign="top">Good framing with the light. I feel that less shadow detail on the two men, particularly on the gentleman on the left, would have made for a quite interesting and mysterious image. But then, that image might have nothign to do with what you wanted to portrait.</td>', 'Good framing with the light. I feel that less shadow detail on the two men, particularly on the gentleman on the left, would have made for a quite interesting and mysterious image. But then, that image might have nothign to do with what you wanted to portrait.', '2015-01-20 18:28:10.000000', NULL, 0),
(7313643, 1137901, 1031, '<td valign="top">I cae across <a href="//www.picturecorrect.com/news/photo-glowing-tent-under-a-winter-sky/" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">this picture</a> in an email and I immediately thought of this one. :-)</td>', 'I cae across this picture in an email and I immediately thought of this one. :-)', '2015-02-07 13:48:00.000000', NULL, 0),
(7399285, 1138223, 25024, '<td valign="top">*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club*<br/> <br/>A somewhat appealing image that meets the challenge.<br/> <br/>The artificial light has, I assume, come from the onboard flash of the camera? I like the shallow DOF, I like the dark background, I like the shapes and composition in general. What I am not keen on is the inevitable hotspots of overblown highlights that very often result from this type of shot using on-camera flash, it rarely gives the sort of results I am after but you have used it for the purpose of this challenge.<br/> <br/>I like the detail of the fibres with the OOF elements against the dark background it makes the image a little more intriguing. Thanks for your submission, Sid</td>', '*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club* A somewhat appealing image that meets the challenge. The artificial light has, I assume, come from the onboard flash of the camera? I like the shallow DOF, I like the dark background, I like the shapes and composition in general. What I am not keen on is the inevitable hotspots of overblown highlights that very often result from this type of shot using on-camera flash, it rarely gives the sort of results I am after but you have used it for the purpose of this challenge. I like the detail of the fibres with the OOF elements against the dark background it makes the image a little more intriguing. Thanks for your submission, Sid', '2015-08-23 08:14:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(7399286, 1137880, 25024, '<td valign="top">*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club*<br/> <br/>An original image that meets the challenge well.<br/> <br/>I like your concept it it fits the challenge very well and your composition is very good, well done. The angle of the light, the very slight cropping and its position within the frame are all ideal for the subject. I like the ice and the water on the bulb it works very well adding another intriguing element to the image.<br/> <br/>What I am not so keen on is the background, I wish it were a more uniform white throughout it would give the image even more impact than it already has. Having said that there may well be people here who prefer it this way, that is just my personal preference.<br/> <br/>I think you have done a great here Marcel, thoroughly deserving of your high score and placing, well done, Sid</td>', '*Hello from Sid and the Critique Club* An original image that meets the challenge well. I like your concept it it fits the challenge very well and your composition is very good, well done. The angle of the light, the very slight cropping and its position within the frame are all ideal for the subject. I like the ice and the water on the bulb it works very well adding another intriguing element to the image. What I am not so keen on is the background, I wish it were a more uniform white throughout it would give the image even more impact than it already has. Having said that there may well be people here who prefer it this way, that is just my personal preference. I think you have done a great here Marcel, thoroughly deserving of your high score and placing, well done, Sid', '2015-08-23 08:23:22.000000', NULL, 0);
COMMIT;
